<!--pages/my/my.wxml-->
<view class="topic">
  Instructions
</view>
<view class="help">
  <view>
    1. Attach the microfluidic patch to the skin.
  </view>
  <view>
    2. Allow sweat to fully wet the sensing zones, then wait an additional 1 minute.
  </view>
  <view>
    3. Take a photo of the patch or select an existing image from your gallery.
  </view>
  <view>
    4. Upload and edit the photo to clearly display all five sensing zones.
  </view>
  <view>
    5. Tap the "Start detection" button to extract the RGB values and view the pH and concentrations of urea, glucose, chloride, and magnesium.
  </view>
</view>

